; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Gravity Balls
; CATEGORY: Animation & Many Turtles
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     many turtles, gravity, arrays, physics, SETSHAPE
; SUMMARY:  Six ball turtles are thrown into the air, fall, bounce lower each time, and are thrown again.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Six turtles wearing the circle shape are tossed up with random
;   speeds. Gravity pulls them down, and every bounce on the floor
;   loses some energy, so the bounces get smaller. They also bounce
;   off the side walls. When all of them have nearly stopped, they
;   are thrown up again. Each ball leaves a faint trail of where it
;   has been.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Press Stop to end it. Change :gravity or :bounciness.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * ARRAYS to keep a speed for each turtle: ITEM and SETITEM
;   * gravity: the downward speed grows a little every frame
;   * losing energy: multiply the speed by :bounciness at each bounce
;   * ASK to move each turtle in turn
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Set :bounciness to 1. Do they ever stop?
;   * Set :gravity to 0.1, like on the Moon.
;   * Make the balls bounce off each other (that is harder!).
; ============================================================

; THROW.ALL gives every ball a place at the bottom and an upward
; push, and wipes the old trails.
to throw.all
  clean
  floor
  for [k 1 6] [
    setitem :k :vx (random -60 60) / 10
    setitem :k :vy (random 100 160) / 10
    ask :k [
      penup setxy -250 + 100 * (:k - 1) -240
      setpencolor item :k :colors
      setshape "circle showturtle
      setpensize 1 pendown
    ]
  ]
end

; FLOOR draws the ground line.
to floor
  setpencolor [80 80 80] setpensize 6
  penup setxy -400 -255 setheading 90 pendown forward 800
end

; MOVE.BALL moves ball :k one frame and outputs its speed, so we can
; tell when everything has settled. The local names are :dx and :dy,
; not :vx and :vy: a local with the same name would hide the arrays.
to move.ball :k
  localmake "dx item :k :vx
  localmake "dy (item :k :vy) - :gravity
  localmake "here ask :k [pos]
  localmake "x (first :here) + :dx
  localmake "y (last :here) + :dy
  ; the floor: put the ball back on it and bounce up, losing energy
  if :y < -240 [make "y -240 make "dy minus :dy * :bounciness make "dx :dx * 0.9]
  ; the walls
  if (abs :x) > 390 [make "dx minus :dx make "x 390 * sign :x]
  setitem :k :vx :dx
  setitem :k :vy :dy
  ask :k [setxy :x :y]
  output (abs :dx) + abs :dy
end

; SIGN outputs 1 for positive numbers and -1 for negative ones.
to sign :n
  output ifelse :n < 0 [-1] [1]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [245 245 250]
make "colors [[230 70 70] [240 160 40] [220 200 40] [70 180 90] [60 140 230] [150 90 220]]
make "vx array 6
make "vy array 6
make "gravity 0.4
make "bounciness 0.75
throw.all
forever [
  make "energy 0
  for [k 1 6] [make "energy :energy + move.ball :k]
  ; When the balls hardly move any more, throw them again.
  if :energy < 6 [wait 30 throw.all]
  wait 1
]
